model_sha256	2342e4c26e1a09371c9d80f616e4a4e89397484e24fa883b5d72298f35060b5f
model_md5	9915a5d2d98f7128d7419c82127fdf08
model_bytes	2742509
format	HNG2 (see tika-ml/tika-ml-chardetect/README.md)
status	final-v112 "R", seed 11, 2026-11-05; trained on gold v1.12

Architecture
  43 classes: 37 legacy/UTF-8 charsets (IBM420/IBM424 as -ltr/-rtl pairs), IBM437, binary,
  UTF-16LE, UTF-16BE, UTF-32LE, UTF-32BE.
  Byte n-grams of order 1, 2 (direct, 2^8 and 2^16 rows) and 3 (hashed, 2^16 rows), 16-dim int8
  rows, counted only in windows holding a byte outside printable ASCII/TAB/LF/CR.
  Column channels: byte at even offset, byte at odd offset, first 512 bytes (256 x 16 each).
  Mean + max pooling, log-count feature, one ReLU hidden layer of 128, raw logits.

Training data (nothing from the 1.2M regression corpus)
  Wikipedia text by language, re-encoded per charset (train buckets; web-symbol, NBSP and ’ injection,
  synthetic DOS screens for IBM437/850/852/866, a per-language floor of 0.5 in sparse Latin classes).
  Gold of record v1.12 (Common Crawl HTML, Common Crawl non-HTML, CC v3) fit part only:
  tier A, re-encoded non-HTML UTF-8 units (weight 0.2); tier B, real legacy-charset bytes (weight 0.2).
  UTF-16LE/BE positives (generated, all scripts, with/without BOM, emoji rates, lengths from 16 bytes,
  even-aligned crops).
  Negatives: generated UTF-32LE/BE rows (own classes); generated binary (NUL records, deflate, bytecode,
  integer arrays, random, executables, scattered NULs) plus the gold v1.12 fit binary-verdict documents
  (1,123) as class "binary".
  Web probes went through the production HTML strip rule (maybeStripHtml, no content type).
  Selection on held-out train-side sets (gold v1.12 train sel split, Wikipedia bucket 8) by a rule fixed
  before training; gold v1.12 dev scored once, after the freeze.  Test and sealed splits and Wikipedia
  buckets 0 and 9 were not read.
